Package: zutoml
Title: Read and Write 'TOML' Documents
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Parses 'TOML' (Tom's Obvious Minimal Language) version 1.0
    documents into ordinary R values and writes R values as 'TOML'. Every
    'TOML' type maps to one R type, including the four date and time types,
    and strings are never reinterpreted. Invalid documents are refused with
    the line and column at fault, under configurable size, depth and item
    limits. Output is deterministic and readable. Conformance is checked
    against the 'toml-test' suite (<https://github.com/toml-lang/toml-test>)
    in both directions. The parser and writer are written in C with no
    system library required.
